#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115399 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114951 :question/id #uuid "99db3f5c-5d6f-5e8e-a31c-a627ddd5c6dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-208" :question/problem "If $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{arcsec } x}{\\textrm{arccsc } x},$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x) = \\textrm{arcsec } x$ and $v(x) = \\textrm{arccsc } x$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\nu'(x) =  \\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}\t\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\tv'(x) = -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\text{arccsc }x-\\text{arcsec }x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}{\\text{ arccsc }}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048842 :topic/difficulty 1.2766246463083966 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428105 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: refere